message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "stochastic-cbam-engine: A Stochastic Framework for Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism Exposure Analysis"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, dependency-free R engine that quantifies exporters' exposure to
  the EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM) as a probability distribution
  rather than a single point estimate. The framework couples firm-level technology
  heterogeneity (lognormal deviation from sector-average emission intensity) with
  correlated stochastic processes for the EU ETS carbon price and the exchange rate,
  and reproduces the benchmark-based free-allocation deduction defined by Regulation
  (EU) 2023/956. It separates the legally taxable emission base from the wider
  supply-chain footprint obtained from multi-regional input-output analysis.
  Developed with a focus on Türkiye's iron and steel sector; the modular design
  extends to other CBAM goods. All computation runs locally: the tool fetches no
  live data and transmits no user data.
type: software
